# BTRS directory scope — controls where BTRS *auto-activates*.
#
# Inside this path (at any depth), BTRS routing turns on automatically at
# session start. Outside it, BTRS stays dormant until you type /btrs.
#
# Explicit invocation always works from any directory — scope only governs
# automatic activation, never availability.
#
# install.sh copies this file to scope.conf on first install. Edit scope.conf,
# not this file. Changes take effect immediately (no reinstall needed).
BTRS_SCOPE="$HOME/PERSONAL"
